FAILURE TRIAGE FOR MCP AND ON-DEVICE DEVELOPMENT

COMMAND NOT FOUND / INCORRECT FLAGS
  help COMMAND
  ls /bin
  cat /man/README
PicoNIX is not full Linux; grep -i is not supported in the
current grep implementation. Use 'grep PATTERN [FILE]'.

CC FAILURE
  cc: unsupported C syntax or output too large
  Check <=1024 B source; no #include/global/for/printf;
  local frame <=256 B, <=16 vars, functions <=16; see /man/languages/c.

ASSEMBLER FAILURE
  as: invalid instruction, label or size
  Check Thumb-1 forms, word alignment, branch span, 32 labels,
  source <=2048 B and output <=2040 code bytes.
  Do NOT run old /tmp/a.out when as fails.

PYTHON FAILURE
  python: syntax/runtime error at statement N
  No import/def/classes/CPython libraries. Check indentation,
  max 2048 B, 64 lines, 16 vars, string/list limits.
  A bare 'python' is REPL and must not run in MCP shell.

MCP RESPONSE BREAKS
  incomplete chunked read = connection closed mid-response.
  May be intermittent with heavy output. Reduce to bounded
  hexdump /dev/shm 0 64 or trace show; check ps and network.
  State-changing command may have already taken effect: verify
  current state before retrying.

NO TASK SLOTS
  ps shows occupied slots. Six user slots total.
  mcpd -> sh -> command can consume several simultaneously.
  Do not kill mcpd if remote access is the only control path.

NO OUTPUT / TIMEOUT
  Check command requires a TTY or keeps running (mem, watch,
  gpio, python REPL, trace follow, servers).
  Replace with a short noninteractive inspection command.
  Command can exceed MCP 3-second timeout or 4096-byte output.
